          ]
        ],
        "text": "{{note 1.2}}, {{note 1.3}} and {{note 1.4}} are the b3, 5th and b7 of {{chord 1}}, and {{note 1.6}} is its root. Bar 2 climbs straight up {{chord 2}} (root, b3, b5, b7), and its top note {{note 2.4}} falls a half step to {{note 2.5}}, the 3rd of {{chord 3}}. {{note 2.7}}, the b7 of the dominant, starts the triplet that leads home."
      },
      {
        "topic": "tensions",
        "notes": [
          [
            1,
            5
          ],
          [
            2,
            6
          ]
        ],
        "text": "{{note 1.5}} is the 9th of {{chord 1}}: with the three notes before it, it forms the major-7th arpeggio a minor 3rd above the root, a rootless minor-9th sound. {{note 2.6}} is the b9 of {{chord 3}}, the dark note that marks the V chord of a minor key."
      },
      {
        "topic": "approach",
        "notes": [
          [
            2,
            8
          ],
          [
            2,
            9
          ]
        ],
        "text": "The last two notes of the triplet, {{note 2.8}} and {{note 2.9}}, sit a half step above and a half step below the b3 of {{chord 4}}: a chromatic enclosure. Over {{chord 3}} they are its 13th and 5th, both in the half-whole diminished scale that suits a b9 dominant, so they pass smoothly while they point at the landing note."
      },
      {
        "topic": "rhythm",
        "notes": [
          [
            1,
            2
          ],
          [
            2,
            7
          ],
          [
            3,
            1
          ]
        ],
        "onsetBeats": [
          1.5,
          4,
          1
        ],
        "text": "The line starts on the 'and' of beat 1 and runs in even eighths until beat 4 of bar 2, where {{note 2.7}} starts an eighth-note triplet: three notes in the time of two. That sudden burst, slurred with two pull-offs, throws the line onto beat 1 of the next chorus, and the landing note is held for three beats."
      },
      {
        "topic": "resolution",
        "notes": [
          [
            3,
            1
          ]
        ],
        "text": "{{note 3.1}} is the b3 of {{chord 4}}, the note that makes the chord minor. The b7 of the dominant ({{note 2.7}}) reaches it by way of the enclosure, a decorated version of the classic 7th-to-3rd resolution, and holding it lets the new chorus begin on a clear, strong note rather than a passing one."
      }
